  "lastName": "Qu",
  "overview": "Haiyan Qu, Ph.D teaches quantitative research methods for M.S. in Health Administration Program and M.S. in Health Informatics Program, and mixed methods for the Graduate Certificate in Applications of Mixed Methods Research.\n\nDr.Qu has been an investigator and methodologist for more than 30 funded research projects spanning various disciplines.  Her research interests focus on addressing health disparities, promoting health equity, enhancing healthcare quality, and conducting patient-centered outcomes research utilizing mixed methods. Her work has been published in various esteemed peer-reviewed journals. Since 2013, Dr.Qu has served as a scientist reviewer on multiple merit review panels at the Patient-Centered Outcomes Research Institute (PCORI). She serves as an Associate Editor for the Journal of Risk Management and Healthcare Policy.",
